WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.129
Film Courage: I know we’re talking about
writing being very practical and business-like

00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:10.270
but it sounds like you really do have to be
your own middle-manager or boss.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:15.390
The stress and unromantic notion of deadlines,
how is this?

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.620
Screenwriter Christine Conradt: Unromantic
notion!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.410
I love that phrase.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:26.220
Deadlines are the things that separate someone
who writes for a hobby from someone who writes

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:31.600
for a living and those are two very different
things.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.559
There is a stress obviously to deadlines but
there is also a relief to deadlines in that

00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:40.789
once you’re done with this project it’s
done.

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:43.730
Once it shoots, you’re off of it.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:48.420
Otherwise when it’s your hobby, it’s sort
of this project that you can work on forever,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.260
sometimes people do work on them forever.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.389
So knowing that you are going to get to the
finish line and then move on to the next thing

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:58.269
helps keep you looking forward and I actually
really enjoy that.

00:00:58.269 --> 00:01:05.070
Once of the things I didn’t like about the
YMCA was dealing with the same issues over

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.920
and over, the same personnel issues.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.500
You know the same two people that you’re
counseling three months ago are back in your

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.700
office and we’re talking about this again.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.880
The same budgets every quarter, you’re putting
them together again.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:16.880
It got really boring.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.842
For me, I love going full force into one project
and then now I’m done.

00:01:21.842 --> 00:01:25.649
I can forget about it and now I am full force
into the next thing.

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:28.329
So that’s the beauty of deadlines.

00:01:28.329 --> 00:01:34.770
Film Courage: Right, because I know you mentioned
you didn’t totally want a day job and I

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.189
get that because it is a lot of the same…whatever
the dynamic is there.

00:01:39.189 --> 00:01:42.840
But then there are new problems with being
on your own because there is like this free

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:48.439
fall that could happen if you keep yourself
on track (which it sounds like you’re excellent

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:49.439
at).

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:50.439
Christine Conradt: I try to be.

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:51.559
Film Courage: Absolutely.

00:01:51.559 --> 00:01:52.560
It sounds like it.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.189
That’s a [major] skill in itself, though.

00:01:55.189 --> 00:02:01.289
Christine Conradt: That is a part you really
have to develop and (again) I always tell

00:02:01.289 --> 00:02:06.979
writers this, you’ve got to view this…because
everyone sees writing as their dream job.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:09.979
And they have this fantasy that they get up
in the morning and they are still in their

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:14.320
pajamas and they’re petting their cats and
they’re writing for two hours and it’s

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.030
a wonderful existence.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.050
And it can be whatever you want it to be.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.550
You’re obviously in control of it.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.720
But you have to approach it like a business.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:31.240
You’re doing it not just because you love
it anymore but also to make money.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.780
There’s that whole other component and if
you can balance them right you can have both.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.120
You can still love it and you can still make
money.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.940
But the money part is a big part of it because
we all have bills to pay.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:49.910
So if that’s not for you, then keep it a
hobby and enjoy the process of writing two

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:53.760
pages a day if that’s what you like to do.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.340
That luxury goes as soon as it becomes a profession.

